{# --- Draft/Edit mode --- #}
Save results by calling **Document_Draft** with a single call. You can set multiple fields in one call.

For each requested resource below, pick or generate **one** value and include it in a single `Document_Draft` call.

{% if 'names' in resources %}
**Names:** Generate ONE clear, descriptive document name. Include `name` in the draft call.
{% endif %}
{% if 'descriptions' in resources %}
**Descriptions:** Write ONE description summarizing what the document contains and how it should be used. Include `description` in the draft call.
{% endif %}
{% if 'files' in resources %}
**Files:** Attach uploaded file IDs. Include `file_ids` (list) in the draft call.
{% endif %}
{% if 'texts' in resources %}
**Texts:** Write inline text blocks. Include `texts` (list of strings) for new content, or `text_ids` (list) to reuse existing text resources.
{% endif %}
{% if 'images' in resources %}
**Images:** Select image IDs from Document_Get. Include `image_ids` (list) in the draft call.
{% endif %}
{% if 'parameter_fields' in resources %}
**Parameter Fields:** First call `Document_Get` to see available Parameter Groups. Then call `Document_Get` again with `parameter_ids` set to the relevant group IDs to see the fields within. Select appropriate field IDs and include `parameter_field_ids` in the draft call.
{% endif %}
{% if 'flags' in resources %}
**Flags:** Pass `flag_ids` (a list of flag option UUIDs) to set document state. Include the document_active flag's `id` from Document_Get to make it available.
{% endif %}
{% if 'departments' in resources %}
**Departments:** Select relevant department IDs from Document_Get. Include `department_ids` in the draft call.
{% endif %}

**IMPORTANT:** Only set the requested resources listed above. Do not add extra fields. Omit all optional fields entirely.
